  "content": {
    "id": "p18-q19-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "A rectangle has dimensions $294\\text{ m}\\times315\\text{ m}$. It is to be tiled with square tiles of equal size. What is the least number of tiles required?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$210$ tiles.",
      "worked": "The fewest tiles are needed when their side length is the greatest common divisor of the rectangle's dimensions.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}294&=2\\times3\\times7^2\\\\315&=3^2\\times5\\times7\\\\\\operatorname{GCD}(294,315)&=3\\times7\\\\\\operatorname{GCD}(294,315)&=21\\end{align*}$$\n\nEach tile has side length $21\\text{ m}$, giving $294\\div21=14$ tiles along one side and $315\\div21=15$ along the other.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Number of tiles}&=14\\times15\\\\\\text{Number of tiles}&=210\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 84
  },
